    "html": "<p>Energy is removed from a liquid in a sealed container at a rate of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W\"></span>. The liquid reaches its freezing point and then <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W\"></span> is doubled. What happens to the rate at which the liquid freezes and to the temperature of the liquid? </p>\n\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Rate at which the liquid freezes</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Temperature</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"A\">\n<td><strong>A.</strong></td>\n<td>Increases</td>\n<td>\n<p>Remains unchanged</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"B\">\n<td><strong>B.</strong></td>\n<td>\n<p>Remains unchanged</p>\n</td>\n<td>Decreases</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"C\">\n<td><strong>C.</strong></td>\n<td>Increases</td>\n<td>Decreases</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"D\">\n<td><strong>D.</strong></td>\n<td>\n<p>Remains unchanged</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>Remains unchanged</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
